.TH W3M 1 "2026-08-29" "w3m-vimium 0.5.3"
.SH NAME
w3m \- a high-performance text-based web browser, pager, and Vimium-enhanced terminal navigator
.SH SYNOPSIS
w3m [OPTION]... [ \fIfile\fP | \fIURL\fP ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This defines appropriate quote strings for nroff and troff
.ds lq \&"
.ds rq \&"
.if t .ds lq ``
.if t .ds rq ''
.\" Just in case these number registers aren't set yet...
.if \nN==0 .nr N 10
.if \nD==0 .nr D 5

\fIw3m\fP is an advanced text-based web browser and pager designed for
terminal power users. It renders HTML documents, tables, frames, forms,
and inline graphics (via \fIw3m-img\fP or sixel/kitty protocols).

This enhanced \fBw3m-vimium\fP edition integrates complete Vimium keyboard
ergonomics, an interactive fuzzy Vomnibar, dynamic Tab switcher, visual
link hints, instant bookmarking, external Neovim form editing, and
smart pagination navigation.

.SH ARGUMENTS

When given one or more command line arguments, \fIw3m\fP will handle
targets according to content type. For web URLs, \fIw3m\fP queries remote
servers via HTTP/HTTPS; for local files, it determines MIME type by extension
or content sniffing.

With no argument, \fIw3m\fP reads from standard input (assumed \f(CWtext/plain\fP).

.SH KEYBINDINGS & VIMIUM EXTENSIONS
\fIw3m-vimium\fP provides standard modal keyboard navigation aligned with
modern browser extensions (Vimium / Qutebrowser) and Vim.

.SS Page Scrolling & Navigation
.TP
\fBj\fP, \fBk\fP
Scroll down / up by one line
.TP
\fBh\fP, \fBl\fP
Scroll left / right by one column
.TP
\fBd\fP, \fBu\fP
Scroll down / up by half a page
.TP
\fBCtrl-f\fP, \fBCtrl-b\fP
Scroll down / up by a full page
.TP
\fBgg\fP, \fBG\fP
Jump to top / bottom of document
.TP
\fB0\fP, \fB$\fP
Jump to leftmost / rightmost edge
.TP
\fBH\fP, \fBL\fP
Go back / forward in browsing history
.TP
\fBr\fP, \fBR\fP
Reload current page / reload bypassing cache

.SS Link Hints & Clipboard Yanking
.TP
\fBf\fP
Activate link hints: display two-letter letter labels over all visible links; type the letters to follow the link in current tab
.TP
\fBF\fP
Activate link hints and open target in a new background tab
.TP
\fByf\fP
Activate link hints and copy target link URL to the system clipboard
.TP
\fByF\fP
Activate link hints and copy target link as Markdown \f(CW[Title](URL)\fP to system clipboard
.TP
\fByy\fP
Copy current page URL to system clipboard
.TP
\fBym\fP
Copy current page as Markdown \f(CW[Title](URL)\fP to system clipboard
.TP
\fBgy\fP
Copy URL of the link under cursor directly to clipboard
.TP
\fBgY\fP
Copy URL and title of link under cursor to clipboard
.TP
\fByc\fP
Smart-yank code block under cursor (automatically strips line numbers and prompts)

.SS Interactive Vomnibar & Bookmarks
.TP
\fBb\fP, \fBo\fP
Open interactive floating \fBVomnibar\fP in current tab. Real-time multi-token fuzzy search across browsing history, bookmarks, open tabs, and search engines. Navigate with \fBj\fP/\fBk\fP, switch mode with \fBTab\fP, jump with \fBEnter\fP, dismiss with \fBEsc\fP
.TP
\fBB\fP, \fBO\fP
Open interactive \fBVomnibar\fP and launch target in a new tab
.TP
\fBga\fP
Instant zero-overhead bookmark: immediately saves current page to \f(CW~/.w3m/bookmark.html\fP without opening external CGI forms
.TP
\fBgb\fP
Open bookmark manager
.TP
\fISearch Engine Prefixes in Vomnibar\fR
Type \fBgh:\fP to search GitHub, \fBwk:\fP for Wikipedia, \fBddg:\fP for DuckDuckGo, \fBbi:\fP for Bing, \fBbd:\fP for Baidu

.SS Tab & Buffer Management
.TP
\fBt\fP
Open new tab with smart URL / query input prompt
.TP
\fBT\fP
Open interactive \fBTab Switcher Vomnibar\fP. Lists all open tabs with index numbers, titles, and URLs. Press \fB1-9\fP to jump instantly, \fB/\fP to filter, \fBd\fP or \fBx\fP to close selected tab
.TP
\fBJ\fP, \fBK\fP, \fBgt\fP, \fBgT\fP
Switch to next / previous tab
.TP
\fB<<\fP, \fB>>\fP
Move current tab one position to the left / right
.TP
\fBx\fP
Close current tab
.TP
\fBX\fP
Restore last closed tab (undo close)
.TP
\fBgxa\fP
Close all other tabs except current
.TP
\fBgx0\fP, \fBgx$\fP
Close all tabs to the left / right of current tab

.SS Form Input & External Editor
.TP
\fBgi\fP
Focus first interactive text input field on the page
.TP
\fB[\fInum\fB]gi\fP
Focus \fInum\fR-th text input field directly
.TP
\fBge\fP
Open current form text area or input field in external \fB$EDITOR\fP (e.g. Neovim), sync text back on save-and-quit
.TP
\fBgE\fP
Edit current page URL in place and open in a new tab

.SS Search & Jumplist
.TP
\fB/\fP, \fB?\fP
Search forward / backward in page
.TP
\fBn\fP, \fBN\fP
Repeat last search forward / backward
.TP
\fB*\fP, \fB#\fP
Search forward / backward for the word currently under cursor
.TP
\fBCtrl-o\fP
Jump backward in document location jump list

.SS Smart Pagination & URL Stepping
.TP
\fB]]\fP
Follow 'next' pagination link (auto-detects Next, >, 下一页, etc.)
.TP
\fB[[\fP
Follow 'previous' pagination link (auto-detects Prev, <, 上一页, etc.)
.TP
\fB]a\fP
Increment trailing integer in current URL by 1 (e.g. page/1 -> page/2)
.TP
\fB[a\fP
Decrement trailing integer in current URL by 1

.SS Menus & Quick Outlines
.TP
\fBgo\fP, \fBgO\fP
Open interactive hierarchical Table of Contents popup menu
.TP
\fBgl\fP, \fBgL\fP
Open interactive Links popup menu list

.SH COMMAND LINE OPTIONS
Command line options are introduced with a single \(lq\-\(rq character and
may take an argument.
.SS General options
.TP
\fB\-B\fP
with no other target defined, use the bookmark page for startup
.TP
\fB\-H\fP
use high-intensity colors
.TP
\fB\-M\fP
monochrome display
.TP
\fB\-no-mouse\fP
deactivate mouse support
.TP
\fB\-num\fP
display each line's number
.TP
\fB\-N\fP
distribute multiple command line arguments to tabs
.TP
\fB\-title\fP, \fB\-title=TERM\fP
use the buffer name as terminal title string
.TP
\fB\-v\fP
with no other target defined, welcome users with a built-in page
.TP
\fB\-W\fP
toggle wrapping mode in searches
.TP
\fB\-X\fP
do not initialize/deinitialize the terminal
.TP
\fB+\fInum\fR
go to line \fInum\fR

.SS Browser options
.TP
\fB\-cols \fInum\fR
with stdout as destination; HTML is rendered to lines of \fInum\fR characters
.TP
\fB\-cookie\fP, \fB\-no-cookie\fP
use stored cookies and accept new ones, or do neither
.TP
\fB\-F\fP
render frames
.TP
\fB\-graph\fP, \fB\-no-graph\fP
use or do not use graphic characters for drawing HTML table and frame borders
.TP
\fB\-header \fIstring\fR
append \fIstring\fR to the HTTP(S) request (syntax: \f(CWVariable: Value\fP)
.TP
\fB\-no-proxy\fP
do not use proxy
.TP
\fB\-post \fIfile\fR
use POST method to upload data defined in \fIfile\fR
.TP
\fB\-4\fP, \fB\-6\fP
IPv4 only / IPv6 only

.SS Text pager & Output options
.TP
\fB\-dump\fP
dump rendered page into stdout
.TP
\fB\-dump_source\fP
dump the page's HTML source code into stdout
.TP
\fB\-dump_head\fP
dump response headers of a HEAD request for a URL into stdout
.TP
\fB\-help\fP
show a summary of compiled-in features and options
.TP
\fB\-version\fP
show version of \fIw3m\fP

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBWWW_HOME\fP
Fallback home URL or file path
.TP
\fBW3M_DIR\fP
User configuration and state directory (defaults to \f(CW~/.w3m\fP)
.TP
\fBEDITOR\fP, \fBVISUAL\fP
Default editor launched for form inputs via \fBge\fP

.SH FILES
.TP
\f(CW~/.w3m/bookmark.html\fP
Default bookmark file (supported by instant \fBga\fP)
.TP
\f(CW~/.w3m/config\fP
User configuration file
.TP
\f(CW~/.w3m/history\fP
Browser navigation history (queried by \fBVomnibar\fP \fBb\fP/\fBo\fP)
.TP
\f(CW~/.w3m/keymap\fP
Custom keybindings file

.SH AUTHOR
Originally created by Akinori ITO. Enhanced with Vimium ergonomics, Vomnibar, and high-performance terminal navigation by the Claw & Wu Wenjie workspace project.
